06.30). The season high was 179.62 in week 4 ([[g:2024-04-7-11]]). In the Toilet Bowl they lost to [[f:3|Kolkata Kommies]] 78.14-140.28 in the Toilet Bowl First Round, then beat [[f:9|Clandestine Ball Busters]] 172.20-138.98 in the Toilet Bowl Semifinal, then beat [[f:4|Win one game]] 134.26-93.00 in the Ninth Place Game and finished 9th. The front office made 24 transactions, 1 of them trades."},{"season":"2025","heading":"2025: BubbaNASTIES","text":"Under Brandon, BubbaNASTIES went 4-10 to finish as the No. 9 seed, scoring 1653.28 points, 9th in the league. Their all-play record of 64-90 suggests a team that was better than its record; schedule luck was worth 1.82 wins against them. [[p:421|Matthew Stafford]] led the club with 311.62 points in 15 starts, followed by [[p:3198|Derrick Henry]] (268.40). The season high was 172.98 in week 17 ([[g:2025-17-4-11]]). In the Toilet Bowl they lost to [[f:10|Maddison Beer’s Boys]] 143.42-162.70 in the Toilet Bowl First Round, then beat [[f:12|Happy Feet]] 133.68-54.60 in the Toilet Bowl Semifinal, then beat [[f:4|Win one game]] 172.98-80.70 in the Ninth Place Game and finished 9th. The front office made 17 transactions, 3 of them trades."},{"season":"2026","heading":"2026: BubbaNASTIES","text":"Through 4 games under Brandon, BubbaNASTIES are 3-1 and 4th in the standings, with 550.00 points (5th). [[p:8183|Brock Purdy]] led the club with 102.48 points in 4 starts, followed by [[p:3198|Derrick Henry]] (99.70). The season high was 175.90 in week 1 ([[g:2026-01-3-11]]). The front office made 5 transactions, 0 of them trades."}]}